Digital has NEVER made a 21066 CPU that was designed for more than 233 or
266 MHz.  300MHz is overclocking as it is.

The 21064 and 21164 chips will NOT fit in a 21066 socket!  It is the 21164
that has been rated for 300+ MHz.  THAT's what we mean by the 400MHz
Multia is a myth.  A 21164 chip will NOT fit in a Multia.

To put it another way... can you fit a PPro into a regular Pentium socket?
No.  End of story.
 
