From pjb27@cam.ac.uk Sat May 10 15:19:43 1997
Message-ID: <9705101104.ZM2171@davros.bwh.com>
Date: Sat, 10 May 1997 20:16:31 +0100 (BST)
From: Philip Blundell <pjb27@cam.ac.uk>
Subject: Re: Another Q about UDB
In-Reply-To: <Pine.BSF.3.95.970510201006.5149A-100000@blue.bad.bris.ac.uk>

On Sat, 10 May 1997, Matt Hamilton wrote:

>   Sorry to bug people about this, and thanks to those that answer my last
> note, but does the UDB *HAVE* to have parity SIMMS?

Yes.  More, it has to have "true parity" 36-bit SIMMs - "logic parity"
ones won't work. 

The parity bits are used for an ECC code that allows the logic in the UDB
to correct all one-bit errors and detect all two-bit errors.

p.

