From beww@intac.com Tue May 13 13:49:15 1997
Message-ID: <199705131746.NAA04939@mailhost.intac.com>
Date: Tue, 13 May 97 13:46:46 -0400
From: Brian E.W. Wood <beww@intac.com>
Subject: Re: SCSI parity/termination on the UDB?

>I'm having problems with adding two external SCSI devices to my UDB.  One
>is a Seagate 1.2gb harddrive and the other is a Pioneer 4x CD-ROM.  I'm
>beginning to wonder if I have a parity or termination problem.  If I only
>attach the hard drive, everything is alright.  The moment I add the CD-ROM
>to the chain, I get random SCSI resets and sense key errors.  I have the
>Multia Service Info booklet, but it doesn't say anything about wether the
>SCSI bus or internal drive is terminated or parity enabled/disabled. 
>Anyone know? I do have proper termination on the last external device and
>none of my ID's conflict (internal ID 0, external HD ID 1, CD-ROM ID 4).

I had various strange problems with the external scsi chain on my UDB at 
first. Upon reading the scsi HOWTO it said that if you were using scsi-II 
or external devices you should be sure to use an active terminator. I 
replaced my passive terminator with a good active one and have had no 
problems since. I am running two external HDDs, a CDROM, a tape drive and 
a scanner.

There was a long thread on SCSI termination on this list recently, check 
the archives. The thread was called "DAT drives and the UDB" or something 
like that.

As always, YMMV

