Subject: Re: Locked /etc/passwd
In-Reply-To: <Pine.LNX.3.96.970521092005.9857B-100000@asimov.lib.uaa.alaska.edu>

I don't know about RedHat, but most unix systems "lock" the passwd
file by creating a file called /etc/ptmp.  If you use the 
    vipw 
command, that program does create that file, until you exit the passwd
file normally.

So check for
   /etc/ptmp
  === Al

