Subject: Re: kzpsa adapter; Digital Contract Service
In-Reply-To: <33834FC4.9AF59DF@news.umkc.edu>

>>> david l nicol said:
> 
> Anyone reading axp-list@redhat know if Digital Contract Service cares what
> software you are running on your Digital hardware?

No, I don't think they *ultimately* care, but:

1. the lowest level (console firmware) would have to be something they
   recognize and know how to work with; ie MILO doesn't fit the bill.
   This is so they can run hardware diagnostics packages that are bootable
   from the DEC-provided consoles (ARC/AlphaBIOS/SRM).

2. if the hardware tests out correctly from a "known" console, and the OS the
   hardware is permitted to run actually *runs* correctly. then there'd be no
   use complaining that LINUX didn't run, as LINUX is not officially supported
   by DEC.

--Jay++

