It looks like Alpha and Intel take different routes after encountering (in
write.c, nfs_updatepage()):

[...]
        /* If wsize is smaller than page size, update and write
         * page synchronously.
         */
        if (NFS_SERVER(inode)->wsize < PAGE_SIZE)
[...]

Taking the "if" leads to muddling up count and offset, but skipping it
doesn't.

Tim.
